<turbo-frame id="repo-content-turbo-frame" target="_top" data-turbo-action="advance" class=""><react-app
  app-name="issues-react"
  initial-path="/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018"
  style="display: block; min-height: calc(100vh - 64px);"
  data-attempted-ssr="true"
  data-ssr="true"
  data-lazy="false"
  data-alternate="false"
  data-data-router-enabled="false"
  data-react-profiling="false"
>
  
  <script type="application/json" data-target="react-app.embeddedData">{"payload":{"preloaded_records":{},"structured_data":{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","headline":"[RFC]: Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism for Efficient Long-Context Decoding","articleBody":"### Motivation.\n\nThis RFC proposes adding **Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism** to vLLM, based on [NVIDIA's Helix paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07120) (July 2025). Helix enables efficient long-context decoding by combining Context Parallelism (sequence sharding) with Tensor Parallelism (head sharding), eliminating KV cache duplication that occurs in traditional Tensor Parallelism when `TP \u003e num_kv_heads`.\n\n**Paper results (NVIDIA):**\n- Up to **1.5× decode latency reduction** at fixed batch size\n- Up to **32× more concurrent users** at same latency target\n- Communication overhead **O(B × H)**, independent of sequence length\n\n**Key benefits for vLLM:**\n- **Eliminates KV cache replication** when TPA \u003e num_kv_heads, improving memory efficiency\n- **Reduces memory pressure** for long-context workloads (256K+ tokens)\n- Enables scaling MLA (DeepSeek) and GQA (Llama, Qwen) models more efficiently\n\n## Motivation\n\n### The Problem: KV Cache Duplication\n\nModern LLMs increasingly use **MLA** (Multi-head Latent Attention) or **GQA** (Grouped Query Attention) to reduce KV cache memory. However, these architectures have few KV heads:\n\n| Model | Attention | KV Heads | Problem with TP=8 |\n|-------|-----------|----------|-------------------|\n| DeepSeek-V2/R1 | MLA | 1 (effective) | 8× KV duplication |\n| Llama-3 70B/405B | GQA | 8 | 1× at TP=8, 4× at TP=32 |\n| Qwen2.5 | GQA | 4-8 | 2-8× duplication |\n\nWhen `TP \u003e num_kv_heads`, traditional TP must **duplicate** the KV cache across GPUs, wasting memory bandwidth during decode.\n\n### vLLM's Current DCP and KV Cache Efficiency\n\nvLLM's Decode Context Parallelism (DCP) helps by sharding KV cache along the sequence dimension. DCP works functionally with any TP/DCP combination, but there's a **KV cache efficiency** consideration:\n\nIn standard DCP with TP=32, K=8, DCP=4:\n- Each DCP rank has TPA=8 Q heads but only HKVP=2 KV heads\n- AllGather Q brings all 32 Q heads to every rank\n- Each rank computes attention for all 32 Q heads against its 2 local KV heads\n- This effectively replicates each KV head 4× across TPA\n\nThis KV replication increases memory pressure for long-context workloads. The replication factor grows as TPA/K increases.\n\n\n### Proposed Change.\n\n\n## Proposed Solution: Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism\n\nHelix decouples attention and FFN parallelism, allowing the same N GPUs to \"twist\" between two configurations each layer:\n\n```\nAttention Phase:  KVP × TPA  (KVP = sequence sharding, TPA = head sharding)\nFFN Phase:        TPF × EP   (standard tensor/expert parallelism)\n```\n\n### Key Difference from DCP\n\n| Aspect            | Standard DCP                | Helix                           |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| Communication     | AllGather Q + ReduceScatter | **All-to-All + LSE**            |\n| Q distribution    | AllGather to all ranks      | Distributed by TPA              |\n| KV efficiency     | Replicates when TPA \u003e K     | **No replication**              |\n| GQA at TP=32, K=8 | Works but 4× KV replication | ✅ No replication (TPA=8, KVP=4) |\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nInput → QKV Proj → FlashAttn (local KV) → All-to-All → LSE Reduction → Output Proj → AllReduce\n        (redundant)  + LSE                 (exchange)   (exact softmax)\n```\n\nThe All-to-All exchanges partial attention outputs with their log-sum-exp (LSE) values, enabling mathematically exact attention reconstruction across KVP ranks.\n\n\n### Feedback Period.\n\n_No response_\n\n### CC List.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Any Other Things.\n\n\n## Roadmap\n\n| Phase | Description | Dependencies |\n|-------|-------------|--------------|\n| **1. Core Helix (MLA)** | All-to-All + LSE reduction for MLA models | None |\n| **2. GQA Support** | Extend Helix to GQA models beyond KV head constraint | Phase 1 |\n| **3. A2A Optimization** | Optimized All-to-All implementation | Phase 1 |\n\nPhase 1 is the prerequisite; Phases 2 and 3 can proceed in parallel.\n\n## Design Principles\n\n1. **Minimal new parameters** - Single `helix_mode` flag; reuse existing `tensor_parallel_size` and `decode_context_parallel_size`\n2. **Reuse DCP infrastructure** - KV interleaving, slot mapping, rank groups all compatible\n3. **Feature parity** - Support same models/backends as DCP\n\n## API Design\n\n```python\nfrom vllm import LLM\n\n# Enable Helix for long-context MLA model\nllm = LLM(\n    model=\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite\",\n    tensor_parallel_size=8,\n    decode_context_parallel_size=4,  # KVP = 4\n    helix_mode=True,                 # Enable Helix (All-to-All)\n)\n\n# For GQA model beyond KV head limit (Phase 2)\nllm = LLM(\n    model=\"meta-llama/Llama-3-70B\",\n    tensor_parallel_size=32,\n    decode_context_parallel_size=4,  # Would not work with standard DCP\n    helix_mode=True,                 # TPA=8, KVP=4\n)\n```\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### 1. Extend DCP to support TP \u003e num_kv_heads\n\nWould require duplicating KV heads across ranks, defeating the purpose of context parallelism.\n\n### 2. Ring attention\n\nHigher latency for decode phase due to sequential send/recv chain. All-to-All provides lower latency when all GPUs have direct connectivity (NVSwitch).\n\n## Related Work\n\n- **Helix Paper:** [arXiv:2507.07120](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07120) - Original Helix parallelism paper (NVIDIA, July 2025)\n- **vLLM DCP:** Existing decode context parallelism in vLLM\n- **Related vLLM RFCs:**\n  - [#22693](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693) - Context Parallelism \u0026\u0026 Sequence Parallelism\n  - [#26133](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133) - Context Parallelism with Fully Sharded KV Cache and Ring Attention\n\n**Differentiation:** While #22693 and #26133 use ring attention for context parallelism, Helix uses **All-to-All** communication which provides lower latency on NVSwitch-connected systems and removes the `TP ≤ num_kv_heads` constraint for GQA models.\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","author":{"url":"https://github.com/sungsooha","@type":"Person","name":"sungsooha"},"datePublished":"2026-02-06T20:23:39.000Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"https://schema.org/CommentAction","userInteractionCount":10},"url":"https://github.com/34018/vllm/issues/34018"},"best_match_sort_enabled":false,"issue_search_type":"ISSUE_HYBRID","preloadedQueries":[{"queryId":"a26f23e2a3f0b937e56dfb64f5b08643","queryName":"IssueViewerViewQuery","variables":{"count":15,"number":34018,"owner":"vllm-project","repo":"vllm"},"result":{"data":{"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","isOwnerEnterpriseManaged":false,"owner":{"__typename":"Organization","userNameDisplayConfiguration":"HANDLE","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw"},"issue":{"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"viewerCanUpdateMetadata":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","databaseId":599547518,"name":"vllm","isArchived":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","viewerCanInteract":false,"viewerInteractionLimitReasonHTML":"","slashCommandsEnabled":false,"visibility":"PUBLIC","viewerCanPush":false,"owner":{"__typename":"Organization","login":"vllm-project","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project","databaseId":136984999,"issueFieldsEnabled":true,"issueFields":{"totalCount":0},"pinnedIssueFields":{"nodes":[]}},"isPrivate":false,"isWritable":true,"isOwnerEnterpriseManaged":false,"viewerCanPinIssues":false,"isCopilotAgentEnabled":null,"issueTypes":{"edges":[{"node":{"id":"IT_kwDOCCo5p84BLcJj"}},{"node":{"id":"IT_kwDOCCo5p84BLcJm"}},{"node":{"id":"IT_kwDOCCo5p84BLcJq"}}]},"pinnedIssues":{"totalCount":3},"viewerIssueCreationPermissions":{"triageable":false}},"updatedAt":"2026-04-22T06:49:45Z","titleHTML":"[RFC]: Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism for Efficient Long-Context Decoding","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018","viewerCanUpdateNext":false,"issueType":null,"duplicateOf":null,"linkedPullRequests":{"nodes":[{"repository":{"name":"vllm","nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","login":"vllm-project","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw"},"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg"},"url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34883","number":34883,"state":"MERGED","isDraft":false,"id":"PR_kwDOI7xefs7Ezw_r"}]},"agentAssignments":[],"closedByPullRequestsReferences":{"nodes":[{"id":"PR_kwDOI7xefs7Ezw_r","number":34883,"url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34883","state":"MERGED","databaseId":3301904363}]},"labels":{"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"MQ"},"edges":[{"node":{"id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABgib6pA","color":"DE9220","name":"RFC","nameHTML":"RFC","description":"","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/labels/RFC","archivedAt":null}}]},"milestone":null,"assignedActors":{"nodes":[]},"locked":false,"viewerCanComment":false,"databaseId":3908310113,"state":"CLOSED","stateReason":"COMPLETED","title":"[RFC]: Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism for Efficient Long-Context Decoding","createdAt":"2026-02-06T20:23:39Z","viewerDidAuthor":false,"author":{"avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634405?u=5885b3c604d462fa7772c21d9c6f8d531ade9fdb\u0026v=4","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU=","profileUrl":"https://github.com/sungsooha","name":"sungsoo ha","__typename":"User"},"body":"### Motivation.\n\nThis RFC proposes adding **Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism** to vLLM, based on [NVIDIA's Helix paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07120) (July 2025). Helix enables efficient long-context decoding by combining Context Parallelism (sequence sharding) with Tensor Parallelism (head sharding), eliminating KV cache duplication that occurs in traditional Tensor Parallelism when `TP \u003e num_kv_heads`.\n\n**Paper results (NVIDIA):**\n- Up to **1.5× decode latency reduction** at fixed batch size\n- Up to **32× more concurrent users** at same latency target\n- Communication overhead **O(B × H)**, independent of sequence length\n\n**Key benefits for vLLM:**\n- **Eliminates KV cache replication** when TPA \u003e num_kv_heads, improving memory efficiency\n- **Reduces memory pressure** for long-context workloads (256K+ tokens)\n- Enables scaling MLA (DeepSeek) and GQA (Llama, Qwen) models more efficiently\n\n## Motivation\n\n### The Problem: KV Cache Duplication\n\nModern LLMs increasingly use **MLA** (Multi-head Latent Attention) or **GQA** (Grouped Query Attention) to reduce KV cache memory. However, these architectures have few KV heads:\n\n| Model | Attention | KV Heads | Problem with TP=8 |\n|-------|-----------|----------|-------------------|\n| DeepSeek-V2/R1 | MLA | 1 (effective) | 8× KV duplication |\n| Llama-3 70B/405B | GQA | 8 | 1× at TP=8, 4× at TP=32 |\n| Qwen2.5 | GQA | 4-8 | 2-8× duplication |\n\nWhen `TP \u003e num_kv_heads`, traditional TP must **duplicate** the KV cache across GPUs, wasting memory bandwidth during decode.\n\n### vLLM's Current DCP and KV Cache Efficiency\n\nvLLM's Decode Context Parallelism (DCP) helps by sharding KV cache along the sequence dimension. DCP works functionally with any TP/DCP combination, but there's a **KV cache efficiency** consideration:\n\nIn standard DCP with TP=32, K=8, DCP=4:\n- Each DCP rank has TPA=8 Q heads but only HKVP=2 KV heads\n- AllGather Q brings all 32 Q heads to every rank\n- Each rank computes attention for all 32 Q heads against its 2 local KV heads\n- This effectively replicates each KV head 4× across TPA\n\nThis KV replication increases memory pressure for long-context workloads. The replication factor grows as TPA/K increases.\n\n\n### Proposed Change.\n\n\n## Proposed Solution: Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism\n\nHelix decouples attention and FFN parallelism, allowing the same N GPUs to \"twist\" between two configurations each layer:\n\n```\nAttention Phase:  KVP × TPA  (KVP = sequence sharding, TPA = head sharding)\nFFN Phase:        TPF × EP   (standard tensor/expert parallelism)\n```\n\n### Key Difference from DCP\n\n| Aspect            | Standard DCP                | Helix                           |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| Communication     | AllGather Q + ReduceScatter | **All-to-All + LSE**            |\n| Q distribution    | AllGather to all ranks      | Distributed by TPA              |\n| KV efficiency     | Replicates when TPA \u003e K     | **No replication**              |\n| GQA at TP=32, K=8 | Works but 4× KV replication | ✅ No replication (TPA=8, KVP=4) |\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nInput → QKV Proj → FlashAttn (local KV) → All-to-All → LSE Reduction → Output Proj → AllReduce\n        (redundant)  + LSE                 (exchange)   (exact softmax)\n```\n\nThe All-to-All exchanges partial attention outputs with their log-sum-exp (LSE) values, enabling mathematically exact attention reconstruction across KVP ranks.\n\n\n### Feedback Period.\n\n_No response_\n\n### CC List.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Any Other Things.\n\n\n## Roadmap\n\n| Phase | Description | Dependencies |\n|-------|-------------|--------------|\n| **1. Core Helix (MLA)** | All-to-All + LSE reduction for MLA models | None |\n| **2. GQA Support** | Extend Helix to GQA models beyond KV head constraint | Phase 1 |\n| **3. A2A Optimization** | Optimized All-to-All implementation | Phase 1 |\n\nPhase 1 is the prerequisite; Phases 2 and 3 can proceed in parallel.\n\n## Design Principles\n\n1. **Minimal new parameters** - Single `helix_mode` flag; reuse existing `tensor_parallel_size` and `decode_context_parallel_size`\n2. **Reuse DCP infrastructure** - KV interleaving, slot mapping, rank groups all compatible\n3. **Feature parity** - Support same models/backends as DCP\n\n## API Design\n\n```python\nfrom vllm import LLM\n\n# Enable Helix for long-context MLA model\nllm = LLM(\n    model=\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite\",\n    tensor_parallel_size=8,\n    decode_context_parallel_size=4,  # KVP = 4\n    helix_mode=True,                 # Enable Helix (All-to-All)\n)\n\n# For GQA model beyond KV head limit (Phase 2)\nllm = LLM(\n    model=\"meta-llama/Llama-3-70B\",\n    tensor_parallel_size=32,\n    decode_context_parallel_size=4,  # Would not work with standard DCP\n    helix_mode=True,                 # TPA=8, KVP=4\n)\n```\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### 1. Extend DCP to support TP \u003e num_kv_heads\n\nWould require duplicating KV heads across ranks, defeating the purpose of context parallelism.\n\n### 2. Ring attention\n\nHigher latency for decode phase due to sequential send/recv chain. All-to-All provides lower latency when all GPUs have direct connectivity (NVSwitch).\n\n## Related Work\n\n- **Helix Paper:** [arXiv:2507.07120](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07120) - Original Helix parallelism paper (NVIDIA, July 2025)\n- **vLLM DCP:** Existing decode context parallelism in vLLM\n- **Related vLLM RFCs:**\n  - [#22693](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693) - Context Parallelism \u0026\u0026 Sequence Parallelism\n  - [#26133](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133) - Context Parallelism with Fully Sharded KV Cache and Ring Attention\n\n**Differentiation:** While #22693 and #26133 use ring attention for context parallelism, Helix uses **All-to-All** communication which provides lower latency on NVSwitch-connected systems and removes the `TP ≤ num_kv_heads` constraint for GQA models.\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","bodyHTML":"\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eMotivation.\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis RFC proposes adding \u003cstrong\u003eHelix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism\u003c/strong\u003e to vLLM, based on \u003ca href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07120\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eNVIDIA's Helix paper\u003c/a\u003e (July 2025). Helix enables efficient long-context decoding by combining Context Parallelism (sequence sharding) with Tensor Parallelism (head sharding), eliminating KV cache duplication that occurs in traditional Tensor Parallelism when \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eTP \u0026gt; num_kv_heads\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePaper results (NVIDIA):\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUp to \u003cstrong\u003e1.5× decode latency reduction\u003c/strong\u003e at fixed batch size\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUp to \u003cstrong\u003e32× more concurrent users\u003c/strong\u003e at same latency target\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCommunication overhead \u003cstrong\u003eO(B × H)\u003c/strong\u003e, independent of sequence length\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKey benefits for vLLM:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEliminates KV cache replication\u003c/strong\u003e when TPA \u0026gt; num_kv_heads, improving memory efficiency\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReduces memory pressure\u003c/strong\u003e for long-context workloads (256K+ tokens)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnables scaling MLA (DeepSeek) and GQA (Llama, Qwen) models more efficiently\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eMotivation\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe Problem: KV Cache Duplication\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eModern LLMs increasingly use \u003cstrong\u003eMLA\u003c/strong\u003e (Multi-head Latent Attention) or \u003cstrong\u003eGQA\u003c/strong\u003e (Grouped Query Attention) to reduce KV cache memory. However, these architectures have few KV heads:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable role=\"table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eModel\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eAttention\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eKV Heads\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eProblem with TP=8\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eDeepSeek-V2/R1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eMLA\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e1 (effective)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e8× KV duplication\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eLlama-3 70B/405B\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eGQA\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e1× at TP=8, 4× at TP=32\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eQwen2.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eGQA\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e4-8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e2-8× duplication\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhen \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eTP \u0026gt; num_kv_heads\u003c/code\u003e, traditional TP must \u003cstrong\u003eduplicate\u003c/strong\u003e the KV cache across GPUs, wasting memory bandwidth during decode.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003evLLM's Current DCP and KV Cache Efficiency\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003evLLM's Decode Context Parallelism (DCP) helps by sharding KV cache along the sequence dimension. DCP works functionally with any TP/DCP combination, but there's a \u003cstrong\u003eKV cache efficiency\u003c/strong\u003e consideration:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIn standard DCP with TP=32, K=8, DCP=4:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEach DCP rank has TPA=8 Q heads but only HKVP=2 KV heads\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAllGather Q brings all 32 Q heads to every rank\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEach rank computes attention for all 32 Q heads against its 2 local KV heads\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThis effectively replicates each KV head 4× across TPA\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis KV replication increases memory pressure for long-context workloads. The replication factor grows as TPA/K increases.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eProposed Change.\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eProposed Solution: Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHelix decouples attention and FFN parallelism, allowing the same N GPUs to \"twist\" between two configurations each layer:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"Attention Phase:  KVP × TPA  (KVP = sequence sharding, TPA = head sharding)\nFFN Phase:        TPF × EP   (standard tensor/expert parallelism)\"\u003e\u003cpre class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eAttention Phase:  KVP × TPA  (KVP = sequence sharding, TPA = head sharding)\nFFN Phase:        TPF × EP   (standard tensor/expert parallelism)\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eKey Difference from DCP\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable role=\"table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eAspect\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eStandard DCP\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eHelix\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eCommunication\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAllGather Q + ReduceScatter\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAll-to-All + LSE\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eQ distribution\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAllGather to all ranks\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eDistributed by TPA\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eKV efficiency\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eReplicates when TPA \u0026gt; K\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNo replication\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eGQA at TP=32, K=8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eWorks but 4× KV replication\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e✅ No replication (TPA=8, KVP=4)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eData Flow\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"Input → QKV Proj → FlashAttn (local KV) → All-to-All → LSE Reduction → Output Proj → AllReduce\n        (redundant)  + LSE                 (exchange)   (exact softmax)\"\u003e\u003cpre class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eInput → QKV Proj → FlashAttn (local KV) → All-to-All → LSE Reduction → Output Proj → AllReduce\n        (redundant)  + LSE                 (exchange)   (exact softmax)\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe All-to-All exchanges partial attention outputs with their log-sum-exp (LSE) values, enabling mathematically exact attention reconstruction across KVP ranks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eFeedback Period.\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eNo response\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eCC List.\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eNo response\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eAny Other Things.\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eRoadmap\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable role=\"table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003ePhase\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eDescription\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eDependencies\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1. Core Helix (MLA)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAll-to-All + LSE reduction for MLA models\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eNone\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2. GQA Support\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eExtend Helix to GQA models beyond KV head constraint\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ePhase 1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e3. A2A Optimization\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eOptimized All-to-All implementation\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ePhase 1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePhase 1 is the prerequisite; Phases 2 and 3 can proceed in parallel.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eDesign Principles\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMinimal new parameters\u003c/strong\u003e - Single \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003ehelix_mode\u003c/code\u003e flag; reuse existing \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003etensor_parallel_size\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003edecode_context_parallel_size\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReuse DCP infrastructure\u003c/strong\u003e - KV interleaving, slot mapping, rank groups all compatible\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFeature parity\u003c/strong\u003e - Support same models/backends as DCP\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eAPI Design\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-python notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"from vllm import LLM\n\n# Enable Helix for long-context MLA model\nllm = LLM(\n    model=\u0026quot;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite\u0026quot;,\n    tensor_parallel_size=8,\n    decode_context_parallel_size=4,  # KVP = 4\n    helix_mode=True,                 # Enable Helix (All-to-All)\n)\n\n# For GQA model beyond KV head limit (Phase 2)\nllm = LLM(\n    model=\u0026quot;meta-llama/Llama-3-70B\u0026quot;,\n    tensor_parallel_size=32,\n    decode_context_parallel_size=4,  # Would not work with standard DCP\n    helix_mode=True,                 # TPA=8, KVP=4\n)\"\u003e\u003cpre class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003evllm\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eLLM\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e# Enable Helix for long-context MLA model\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003ellm\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eLLM\u003c/span\u003e(\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003emodel\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite\"\u003c/span\u003e,\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003etensor_parallel_size\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e8\u003c/span\u003e,\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003edecode_context_parallel_size\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e,  \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e# KVP = 4\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003ehelix_mode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eTrue\u003c/span\u003e,                 \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e# Enable Helix (All-to-All)\u003c/span\u003e\n)\n\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e# For GQA model beyond KV head limit (Phase 2)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003ellm\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eLLM\u003c/span\u003e(\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003emodel\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\"meta-llama/Llama-3-70B\"\u003c/span\u003e,\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003etensor_parallel_size\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e32\u003c/span\u003e,\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003edecode_context_parallel_size\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e,  \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e# Would not work with standard DCP\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003ehelix_mode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eTrue\u003c/span\u003e,                 \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e# TPA=8, KVP=4\u003c/span\u003e\n)\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eAlternatives Considered\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003e1. Extend DCP to support TP \u0026gt; num_kv_heads\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWould require duplicating KV heads across ranks, defeating the purpose of context parallelism.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003e2. Ring attention\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHigher latency for decode phase due to sequential send/recv chain. All-to-All provides lower latency when all GPUs have direct connectivity (NVSwitch).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eRelated Work\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHelix Paper:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07120\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003earXiv:2507.07120\u003c/a\u003e - Original Helix parallelism paper (NVIDIA, July 2025)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003evLLM DCP:\u003c/strong\u003e Existing decode context parallelism in vLLM\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRelated vLLM RFCs:\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693/hovercard\"\u003e#22693\u003c/a\u003e - Context Parallelism \u0026amp;\u0026amp; Sequence Parallelism\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133/hovercard\"\u003e#26133\u003c/a\u003e - Context Parallelism with Fully Sharded KV Cache and Ring Attention\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDifferentiation:\u003c/strong\u003e While \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3312280381\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693\"\u003e#22693\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3478786804\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133\"\u003e#26133\u003c/a\u003e use ring attention for context parallelism, Helix uses \u003cstrong\u003eAll-to-All\u003c/strong\u003e communication which provides lower latency on NVSwitch-connected systems and removes the \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eTP ≤ num_kv_heads\u003c/code\u003e constraint for GQA models.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eBefore submitting a new issue...\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul class=\"contains-task-list\"\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"task-list-item\"\u003e\u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"\u003e Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the \u003ca href=\"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003edocumentation page\u003c/a\u003e, which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","bodyVersion":"a1f4b96fdc796d05a4f616436501a04b8d068fae5814d4d1ee483af94024f41b","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"pinnedIssueComment":null,"viewerCanAssign":false,"viewerCanLabel":false,"projectItems":{"edges":[],"pageInfo":{"endCursor":null,"hasNextPage":false}},"viewerCanSetMilestone":false,"isPinned":false,"viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanTransfer":false,"viewerCanConvertToDiscussion":false,"viewerCanLock":false,"viewerCanType":false,"viewerCanSetFields":false,"issueFieldValues":{"nodes":[]},"subIssuesSummary":{"total":0,"completed":0},"pendingSuggestions":[],"frontTimelineItems":{"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnbPyV2gAqjQyOTQxNTY0MzI="},"totalCount":12,"edges":[{"node":{"__typename":"LabeledEvent","__isTimelineEvent":"LabeledEvent","databaseId":22599015877,"createdAt":"2026-02-06T20:23:40Z","actor":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU=","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634405?s=64\u0026u=5885b3c604d462fa7772c21d9c6f8d531ade9fdb\u0026v=4","login":"sungsooha","profileResourcePath":"/sungsooha","__typename":"User","name":"sungsoo ha"},"label":{"id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABgib6pA","archivedAt":null,"nameHTML":"RFC","name":"RFC","color":"DE9220","description":""},"id":"LE_lADOI7xefs7o9BRhzwAAAAVDAZ3F","intent":null,"__isNode":"LabeledEvent"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnDSf5OABqzIyNTk5MDE1ODc3"},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3863493116,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"pisceskkk","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41200699?u=9a2fbd98982afaa49ac63fb3674e24c80733b971\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/pisceskkk","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMjAwNjk5","name":"Qiu Chunshuo"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7mSDn8","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3863493116","createdAt":"2026-02-07T03:40:50Z","authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2026-02-09T01:02:00Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"editor":{"__typename":"User","url":"https://github.com/pisceskkk","login":"pisceskkk","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMjAwNjk5"},"id":"UCE_lALOI7xefs7mSDn8zpcavZg"},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Thanks for the RFC! \n\n\u003e However, DCP's AllGather + ReduceScatter communication pattern requires TP ≤ num_kv_heads for the attention output correction to work correctly.\n\nHowever, I noticed that you mentioned GQA's DCP does not support TP=32, K=8. In fact, DCP can take a value of 4 in this scenario, where HKVP and DCP appear to behave consistently. \nSo I think there is no TP ≤ num_kv_heads constraint for GQA when using DCP. Or perhaps you mean when TP \u003e num_q_heads? \n\n~~Actually, the following line of code is indeed a bit confusing to me. IIUC, the Q within the KVP group is not consistent in the head dimension, right? Could you provide some accuracy data regarding this?~~\n\n~~https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34024/changes#diff-bafd6bd048c5ca7bad726e6f509fe4409f4033342e2b5b0c3016156e2f708b12R833~~\n\n\nAdditionally, in the PCP RFC #25749, we have planned to use all2all for communication in DCP, as detailed in the flowchart of the PCP decode stage. In fact, this is also how we have implemented it in vLLM-Ascend for NPU. I believe it would be advisable to replace DCP communication with all2all in vLLM as well.\n\nhttps://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/blob/main/vllm_ascend/attention/context_parallel/attention_cp.py#L784-L797\n","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThanks for the RFC!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHowever, DCP's AllGather + ReduceScatter communication pattern requires TP ≤ num_kv_heads for the attention output correction to work correctly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHowever, I noticed that you mentioned GQA's DCP does not support TP=32, K=8. In fact, DCP can take a value of 4 in this scenario, where HKVP and DCP appear to behave consistently.\u003cbr\u003e\nSo I think there is no TP ≤ num_kv_heads constraint for GQA when using DCP. Or perhaps you mean when TP \u0026gt; num_q_heads?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cdel\u003eActually, the following line of code is indeed a bit confusing to me. IIUC, the Q within the KVP group is not consistent in the head dimension, right? Could you provide some accuracy data regarding this?\u003c/del\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cdel\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34024/changes#diff-bafd6bd048c5ca7bad726e6f509fe4409f4033342e2b5b0c3016156e2f708b12R833\"\u003ehttps://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34024/changes#diff-bafd6bd048c5ca7bad726e6f509fe4409f4033342e2b5b0c3016156e2f708b12R833\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/del\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eAdditionally, in the PCP RFC \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3456199147\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/25749\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/25749/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/25749\"\u003e#25749\u003c/a\u003e, we have planned to use all2all for communication in DCP, as detailed in the flowchart of the PCP decode stage. In fact, this is also how we have implemented it in vLLM-Ascend for NPU. I believe it would be advisable to replace DCP communication with all2all in vLLM as well.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/blob/main/vllm_ascend/attention/context_parallel/attention_cp.py#L784-L797\"\u003ehttps://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/blob/main/vllm_ascend/attention/context_parallel/attention_cp.py#L784-L797\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"9bb0b6cba2e03de001f8d7a1322a16ecde38097abc671aef834015652a88c6e3","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnDYwIdAAqjM4NjM0OTMxMTY="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3868357953,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"LucasWilkinson","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8854186?u=ea09464ea9d1523f09aa799c293fb42455410c54\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTQxODY=","name":"Lucas Wilkinson"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7mknVB","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3868357953","createdAt":"2026-02-08T21:46:40Z","authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2026-02-12T17:16:34Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"editor":{"__typename":"User","url":"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson","login":"LucasWilkinson","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTQxODY="},"id":"UCE_lALOI7xefs7mknVBzph2rWg"},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Thanks for the RFC! We appreciate the contribution.\n\nI think we should fold these improvements into DCP rather than introducing new naming/modes; which just adds to the mental burden for users and developers. Based on my reading of this RFC the main additions are:\n\n1) All-to-All instead of AG+RS for output combination\n  - We should benchmark this. If AG+RS has value on certain cases, add `--dcp-comm-backend {ag_rs, a2a}`; otherwise just make A2A the default and rip out AG+RS (hopefully this is the case as @pisceskkk pointed out).\n\n2) Q proj weight replication across DCP siblings to skip AllGather Q\n  - We should just add a `--dcp-replicate-q-proj` flag (and assert if `--dcp-comm-backend` is not a2a)\n  - Worth benchmarking to see if this should be default.\n\n3) Seperating the TP size for attention and FFN layers\n  - This has been brought up before in other contexts before beyond DCP (e.g. for a 16 GPU deployment someone might want to do: { attention: TPA=4 x DP=4, ffn/moe: TP=1 x EP }); seems valuable :+1:. However, I think we should create a seperate RFC for this so we can design the UX more holistically and engage the broader community. I would assume this would be `-tpa=N` or something like that.\n\nPlease let me know if I am missing something.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThanks for the RFC! We appreciate the contribution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI think we should fold these improvements into DCP rather than introducing new naming/modes; which just adds to the mental burden for users and developers. Based on my reading of this RFC the main additions are:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAll-to-All instead of AG+RS for output combination\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWe should benchmark this. If AG+RS has value on certain cases, add \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-comm-backend {ag_rs, a2a}\u003c/code\u003e; otherwise just make A2A the default and rip out AG+RS (hopefully this is the case as \u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/pisceskkk/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/pisceskkk\"\u003e@pisceskkk\u003c/a\u003e pointed out).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003col start=\"2\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eQ proj weight replication across DCP siblings to skip AllGather Q\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWe should just add a \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-replicate-q-proj\u003c/code\u003e flag (and assert if \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-comm-backend\u003c/code\u003e is not a2a)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWorth benchmarking to see if this should be default.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003col start=\"3\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSeperating the TP size for attention and FFN layers\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThis has been brought up before in other contexts before beyond DCP (e.g. for a 16 GPU deployment someone might want to do: { attention: TPA=4 x DP=4, ffn/moe: TP=1 x EP }); seems valuable 👍. However, I think we should create a seperate RFC for this so we can design the UX more holistically and engage the broader community. I would assume this would be \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e-tpa=N\u003c/code\u003e or something like that.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePlease let me know if I am missing something.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"0c64a618c826a729ad3eb3518d665fbfef0938f16b8562b983284a7461476eda","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnD84mgAAqjM4NjgzNTc5NTM="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3873299087,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634405?u=5885b3c604d462fa7772c21d9c6f8d531ade9fdb\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU=","name":"sungsoo ha"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7m3dqP","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3873299087","createdAt":"2026-02-09T18:35:55Z","authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Thanks @pisceskkk  and @LucasWilkinson for the thoughtful feedback!\n\n## Clarification on the constraint (@pisceskkk )\n\nYou're right - my wording was imprecise. DCP does work functionally with TP=32, K=8 when DCP=4. The constraint I meant to describe is about **KV cache efficiency**, not functional incompatibility.\n\nIn standard DCP with TP=32, K=8, DCP=4:\n- Each DCP rank has TPA=8 Q heads but only HKVP=2 KV heads\n- AllGather Q brings all 32 Q heads to every rank\n- Each rank computes attention for all 32 Q heads against its 2 local KV heads\n- This effectively replicates each KV head 4x across TPA\n\nThe contribution here is eliminating this replication by:\n1. Distributing Q heads by TPA (not full TP) so each rank only has its local Q heads\n2. Skipping AllGather Q - each rank computes only its TPA heads against local KV\n3. Using A2A + LSE to combine partial results across KVP groups\n\nI'll update the RFC to clarify this. Thanks for pointing to PCP RFC #25749 and vLLM-Ascend - great to see A2A is already proven in the vLLM ecosystem!\n\n## On folding into DCP (@LucasWilkinson )\n\nI agree with your approach to fold these into DCP rather than a separate \"Helix mode\".\n\n**Benchmark Context:**\n\nIt's worth noting that the Helix paper and TensorRT-LLM compare against pure TP (no context parallelism), showing significant latency improvements. In vLLM, standard DCP already captures the latency benefits from KV cache sharding - so our comparison is against a stronger baseline.\n\n**E2E Results (H200 8-GPU, DeepSeek-V2-Lite MLA):**\n\n| Context | pure_tp | DCP | Improvement |\n|---------|---------|-----|-------------|\n| 256K | 8.77 ms | 5.25 ms | **-40%** |\n| 512K | 14.34 ms | 6.01 ms | **-58%** |\n| 1M | 25.48 ms | 7.42 ms | **-71%** |\n\n**A2A vs AG+RS:**\n\nA2A and AG+RS show **comparable latency** in our benchmarks. The primary benefit of the A2A approach is **memory efficiency**: by distributing Q heads by TPA and skipping AllGather Q, we eliminate KV cache replication when TPA \u003e num_kv_heads. This reduces memory pressure for long-context workloads.\n\nAdditionally, A2A establishes a foundation for future optimization. TensorRT-LLM achieves better A2A performance using custom CUDA kernels + MNNVL (direct NVLink access). We have a roadmap to explore similar optimizations.\n\n**Summary of contribution:**\n- **Memory efficiency**: No KV replication when TPA \u003e K (unique benefit)\n- **Performance**: Comparable to standard DCP (no regression)\n- **Foundation**: A2A pattern enables future optimization\n\nGiven this, supporting both options via `--dcp-comm-backend {ag_rs, a2a}` provides flexibility. Open to community input on the default.\n\n**Q replication (`--dcp-replicate-q`):**\n\nThis makes sense. For MLA models (effectively K=1), Q replication is needed. For GQA, skipping AllGather Q provides the memory benefit (no KV replication when TPA \u003e K).\n\n**TPA/TP separation:**\n\nHappy to discuss TPA separation further here. Let me know if you'd prefer a separate RFC for broader design discussion.\n\n## Proposed path forward\n\n1. Update PR to use DCP-based flags instead of `--helix-mode`\n2. Keep both AG+RS and A2A options (default TBD based on community input)\n3. Continue TPA design discussion here or in separate RFC per your preference\n\nDoes this align with what you had in mind?","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThanks \u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/pisceskkk/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/pisceskkk\"\u003e@pisceskkk\u003c/a\u003e  and \u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/LucasWilkinson/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson\"\u003e@LucasWilkinson\u003c/a\u003e for the thoughtful feedback!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eClarification on the constraint (\u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/pisceskkk/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/pisceskkk\"\u003e@pisceskkk\u003c/a\u003e )\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eYou're right - my wording was imprecise. DCP does work functionally with TP=32, K=8 when DCP=4. The constraint I meant to describe is about \u003cstrong\u003eKV cache efficiency\u003c/strong\u003e, not functional incompatibility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIn standard DCP with TP=32, K=8, DCP=4:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEach DCP rank has TPA=8 Q heads but only HKVP=2 KV heads\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAllGather Q brings all 32 Q heads to every rank\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEach rank computes attention for all 32 Q heads against its 2 local KV heads\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThis effectively replicates each KV head 4x across TPA\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe contribution here is eliminating this replication by:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDistributing Q heads by TPA (not full TP) so each rank only has its local Q heads\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSkipping AllGather Q - each rank computes only its TPA heads against local KV\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUsing A2A + LSE to combine partial results across KVP groups\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI'll update the RFC to clarify this. Thanks for pointing to PCP RFC \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3456199147\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/25749\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/25749/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/25749\"\u003e#25749\u003c/a\u003e and vLLM-Ascend - great to see A2A is already proven in the vLLM ecosystem!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eOn folding into DCP (\u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/LucasWilkinson/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson\"\u003e@LucasWilkinson\u003c/a\u003e )\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI agree with your approach to fold these into DCP rather than a separate \"Helix mode\".\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBenchmark Context:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIt's worth noting that the Helix paper and TensorRT-LLM compare against pure TP (no context parallelism), showing significant latency improvements. In vLLM, standard DCP already captures the latency benefits from KV cache sharding - so our comparison is against a stronger baseline.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eE2E Results (H200 8-GPU, DeepSeek-V2-Lite MLA):\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable role=\"table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eContext\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003epure_tp\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eDCP\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eImprovement\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e256K\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e8.77 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e5.25 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e-40%\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e512K\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e14.34 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e6.01 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e-58%\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e1M\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e25.48 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e7.42 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e-71%\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA2A vs AG+RS:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eA2A and AG+RS show \u003cstrong\u003ecomparable latency\u003c/strong\u003e in our benchmarks. The primary benefit of the A2A approach is \u003cstrong\u003ememory efficiency\u003c/strong\u003e: by distributing Q heads by TPA and skipping AllGather Q, we eliminate KV cache replication when TPA \u0026gt; num_kv_heads. This reduces memory pressure for long-context workloads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eAdditionally, A2A establishes a foundation for future optimization. TensorRT-LLM achieves better A2A performance using custom CUDA kernels + MNNVL (direct NVLink access). We have a roadmap to explore similar optimizations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSummary of contribution:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMemory efficiency\u003c/strong\u003e: No KV replication when TPA \u0026gt; K (unique benefit)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePerformance\u003c/strong\u003e: Comparable to standard DCP (no regression)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFoundation\u003c/strong\u003e: A2A pattern enables future optimization\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eGiven this, supporting both options via \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-comm-backend {ag_rs, a2a}\u003c/code\u003e provides flexibility. Open to community input on the default.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQ replication (\u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-replicate-q\u003c/code\u003e):\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis makes sense. For MLA models (effectively K=1), Q replication is needed. For GQA, skipping AllGather Q provides the memory benefit (no KV replication when TPA \u0026gt; K).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTPA/TP separation:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHappy to discuss TPA separation further here. Let me know if you'd prefer a separate RFC for broader design discussion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 dir=\"auto\"\u003eProposed path forward\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdate PR to use DCP-based flags instead of \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--helix-mode\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eKeep both AG+RS and A2A options (default TBD based on community input)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eContinue TPA design discussion here or in separate RFC per your preference\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eDoes this align with what you had in mind?\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"952c3cf99931fd669afa6a1e15327d2f6cea4130c8e569d7ecde8d1910fea8ca","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnEOwUvgAqjM4NzMyOTkwODc="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3875037581,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"gjc0824","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63247409?v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/gjc0824","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjQ3NDA5","name":"Jingchun Gao"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7m-GGN","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3875037581","createdAt":"2026-02-10T02:56:26Z","authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Thanks for the RFC! But I am confused about the performance data. \n\n\u003e \nE2E Results (H200 8-GPU, DeepSeek-V2-Lite MLA):\nContext | pure_tp | DCP | Improvement\n-- | -- | -- | --\n256K | 8.77 ms | 5.25 ms | -40%\n512K | 14.34 ms | 6.01 ms | -58%\n1M | 25.48 ms | 7.42 ms | -71%\n\nWhat exactly does E2E result refer to? Is it the decode performance of the historical KV based on the corresponding context? May I understand this as TPOT(Time Per Output Token)?\n","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThanks for the RFC! But I am confused about the performance data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eE2E Results (H200 8-GPU, DeepSeek-V2-Lite MLA):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable role=\"table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eContext\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003epure_tp\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eDCP\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eImprovement\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e256K\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e8.77 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e5.25 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e-40%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e512K\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e14.34 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e6.01 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e-58%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e1M\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e25.48 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e7.42 ms\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e-71%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhat exactly does E2E result refer to? Is it the decode performance of the historical KV based on the corresponding context? May I understand this as TPOT(Time Per Output Token)?\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"7b3400a88c3df5081651bc70d76638d08789682065b5b1498c8e30b8debc5d13","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnEV6j5AAqjM4NzUwMzc1ODE="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3875120771,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634405?u=5885b3c604d462fa7772c21d9c6f8d531ade9fdb\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU=","name":"sungsoo ha"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7m-aaD","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3875120771","createdAt":"2026-02-10T03:31:05Z","authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Yes, exactly - it's **median TPOT (Time Per Output Token)** for decode with the specified context length in KV cache.\n\nBenchmark setup: `vllm bench serve` with 20 prompts × 1024 output tokens at concurrency=1.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eYes, exactly - it's \u003cstrong\u003emedian TPOT (Time Per Output Token)\u003c/strong\u003e for decode with the specified context length in KV cache.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eBenchmark setup: \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003evllm bench serve\u003c/code\u003e with 20 prompts × 1024 output tokens at concurrency=1.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"f6e984fc21802df0a0ff0e993ebf1a476827285a8419ade13ce351faea1c9f93","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnEWaSKgAqjM4NzUxMjA3NzE="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3880515582,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634405?u=5885b3c604d462fa7772c21d9c6f8d531ade9fdb\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU=","name":"sungsoo ha"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7nS_f-","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3880515582","createdAt":"2026-02-10T20:23:53Z","authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Hi @LucasWilkinson - wanted to follow up with an updated development plan based on recent discussions.\n\nI'm breaking down the initial PR into smaller, focused pieces to make review easier:\n\n**Phase 1: MLA Support** (updating current PR)\n- Helix parallelism for MLA models (DeepSeek-V2/V3)\n- Full CUDA graph support\n- Will include both AG+RS and A2A options as discussed\n\n**Phase 2: GQA Support** (separate PR, can run in parallel)\n- Helix for GQA models, starting with Llama\n- Extend to other GQA models in follow-ups\n\n**Phase 3: A2A Optimization** (separate PR, parallel track)\n- Custom A2A kernel\n- MNNVL support for direct NVLink access\n- Target: address the NCCL A2A overhead\n\nThis way we can get MLA support merged first while iterating on GQA and A2A optimization separately. Let me know if this aligns with what you had in mind, or if you'd suggest a different breakdown!","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/LucasWilkinson/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson\"\u003e@LucasWilkinson\u003c/a\u003e - wanted to follow up with an updated development plan based on recent discussions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI'm breaking down the initial PR into smaller, focused pieces to make review easier:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 1: MLA Support\u003c/strong\u003e (updating current PR)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHelix parallelism for MLA models (DeepSeek-V2/V3)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFull CUDA graph support\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWill include both AG+RS and A2A options as discussed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 2: GQA Support\u003c/strong\u003e (separate PR, can run in parallel)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHelix for GQA models, starting with Llama\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eExtend to other GQA models in follow-ups\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 3: A2A Optimization\u003c/strong\u003e (separate PR, parallel track)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCustom A2A kernel\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMNNVL support for direct NVLink access\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTarget: address the NCCL A2A overhead\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis way we can get MLA support merged first while iterating on GQA and A2A optimization separately. Let me know if this aligns with what you had in mind, or if you'd suggest a different breakdown!\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"2476b638e56dff05c2a4ea7fe17fde5af7e2bf17258e5c0c721d1e105688f614","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"__typename":"User","__isActor":"User","login":"pisceskkk","name":"Qiu Chunshuo","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41200699?s=64\u0026u=9a2fbd98982afaa49ac63fb3674e24c80733b971\u0026v=4","__isNode":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMjAwNjk5"}]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnEk5h6gAqjM4ODA1MTU1ODI="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3882047105,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"LucasWilkinson","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8854186?u=ea09464ea9d1523f09aa799c293fb42455410c54\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTQxODY=","name":"Lucas Wilkinson"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7nY1aB","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3882047105","createdAt":"2026-02-11T04:25:36Z","authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"@sungsooha sounds good! thanks for the update!\n\n\u003e Continue TPA design discussion here or in separate RFC per your preference\n\nLets open a separate RFC :+1: that we can socialize more widely ","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/sungsooha/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/sungsooha\"\u003e@sungsooha\u003c/a\u003e sounds good! thanks for the update!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eContinue TPA design discussion here or in separate RFC per your preference\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eLets open a separate RFC 👍 that we can socialize more widely\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"c77261430ad66ba9254117f78f916204014ca3e91fb76a0a51ebb61c2eb8aa4b","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnEryjgAAqjM4ODIwNDcxMDU="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3892257279,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"LucasWilkinson","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8854186?u=ea09464ea9d1523f09aa799c293fb42455410c54\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTQxODY=","name":"Lucas Wilkinson"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7n_yH_","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3892257279","createdAt":"2026-02-12T17:18:46Z","authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2026-02-12T17:19:09Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"editor":{"__typename":"User","url":"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson","login":"LucasWilkinson","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTQxODY="},"id":"UCE_lALOI7xefs7n_yH_zph26Ww"},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"@sungsooha in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444 i see you wrote \n\n\u003e Explicit --dcp-replicate-q flag\n\u003e Considered but rejected because Q replication is fully determined by model architecture:\n\u003e MLA: Always needs Q replication (auto-detect)\n\u003e GQA: Never needs Q replication with A2A (the benefit)\n\u003e No user scenario benefits from explicit control\n\nI apologies there seems to be a miscommunication, I should have been a bit more explicit. What a meant was have a flag `--dcp-replicate-q` (probably better named `--dcp-replicate-q-proj`) that means we replicate Q-proj instead of doing a all-gather of Q (i.e. trading redundant computation and vram for  less communication, we should expose this tradeoff to the user)","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/sungsooha/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/sungsooha\"\u003e@sungsooha\u003c/a\u003e in \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3932952443\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444\"\u003e#34444\u003c/a\u003e i see you wrote\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eExplicit --dcp-replicate-q flag\u003cbr\u003e\nConsidered but rejected because Q replication is fully determined by model architecture:\u003cbr\u003e\nMLA: Always needs Q replication (auto-detect)\u003cbr\u003e\nGQA: Never needs Q replication with A2A (the benefit)\u003cbr\u003e\nNo user scenario benefits from explicit control\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI apologies there seems to be a miscommunication, I should have been a bit more explicit. What a meant was have a flag \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-replicate-q\u003c/code\u003e (probably better named \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-replicate-q-proj\u003c/code\u003e) that means we replicate Q-proj instead of doing a all-gather of Q (i.e. trading redundant computation and vram for  less communication, we should expose this tradeoff to the user)\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"cb3e764db8f9fd06b28186de7e05b513087787a0560c53e9f820f43c91a96c33","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnFLcxPAAqjM4OTIyNTcyNzk="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":3893604140,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634405?u=5885b3c604d462fa7772c21d9c6f8d531ade9fdb\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU=","name":"sungsoo ha"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7oE68s","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-3893604140","createdAt":"2026-02-12T21:54:37Z","authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2026-02-12T21:55:05Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"editor":{"__typename":"User","url":"https://github.com/sungsooha","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"UCE_lALOI7xefs7oE68szpiOO7g"},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"  Thanks for the endorsement on the phased approach, @LucasWilkinson!\n\n  Per your feedback on #34444, I've moved the Q-proj replication discussion here to #34018. Here's the proposed design:\n\n  ---\n\n  ### New Parameter: `--dcp-replicate-q-proj`\n\n  | Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n  |-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n  | `--dcp-replicate-q-proj` | `bool` | `false` | Replicate Q projection instead of AllGather Q |\n\n  **The Tradeoff:**\n\n  | Approach | Communication | Compute | Memory |\n  |----------|---------------|---------|--------|\n  | AllGather Q (default) | Higher (gather Q tensors) | Normal | Normal |\n  | Replicate Q-proj | **Lower** (no Q gather) | **Higher** (redundant Q-proj) | **Higher** (Q-proj weights) |\n\n  **When to use `--dcp-replicate-q-proj`:**\n  - Communication-bound scenarios (slow interconnect)\n  - When compute is cheap relative to communication\n  - Models with small Q projection (overhead is minimal)\n\n  **Constraint:** `--dcp-replicate-q-proj` requires `--dcp-comm-backend a2a` (cannot skip AllGather Q with AG+RS pattern)\n\n  **Data Flow:**\n\n  Without --dcp-replicate-q-proj:\n```\n    Hidden → Q-proj (local) → AllGather Q → Attention → A2A → LSE-reduce\n```\n\n  With --dcp-replicate-q-proj:\n```\n    Hidden → [Replicated Q-proj on all ranks] → Attention → A2A → LSE-reduce\n             ↑ Skip AllGather, but compute Q-proj redundantly\n```\n\n  **Implementation phase:** This would be Phase 2 (after `--dcp-comm-backend` in Phase 1 / PR #34024).\n\n  ---\n\n  I've also updated #34444 to focus purely on the `-tpa` parameter design (see comment there). Let me know if this breakdown works!","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThanks for the endorsement on the phased approach, \u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/LucasWilkinson/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/LucasWilkinson\"\u003e@LucasWilkinson\u003c/a\u003e!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePer your feedback on \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3932952443\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444\"\u003e#34444\u003c/a\u003e, I've moved the Q-proj replication discussion here to \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3908310113\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018\"\u003e#34018\u003c/a\u003e. Here's the proposed design:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eNew Parameter: \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-replicate-q-proj\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable role=\"table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eParameter\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eType\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eDefault\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eDescription\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-replicate-q-proj\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003ebool\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003efalse\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eReplicate Q projection instead of AllGather Q\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe Tradeoff:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable role=\"table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eApproach\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eCommunication\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eCompute\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eMemory\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAllGather Q (default)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eHigher (gather Q tensors)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eNormal\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eNormal\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eReplicate Q-proj\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLower\u003c/strong\u003e (no Q gather)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHigher\u003c/strong\u003e (redundant Q-proj)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHigher\u003c/strong\u003e (Q-proj weights)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhen to use \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-replicate-q-proj\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCommunication-bound scenarios (slow interconnect)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen compute is cheap relative to communication\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eModels with small Q projection (overhead is minimal)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConstraint:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-replicate-q-proj\u003c/code\u003e requires \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-comm-backend a2a\u003c/code\u003e (cannot skip AllGather Q with AG+RS pattern)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eData Flow:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWithout --dcp-replicate-q-proj:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    Hidden → Q-proj (local) → AllGather Q → Attention → A2A → LSE-reduce\"\u003e\u003cpre class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e    Hidden → Q-proj (local) → AllGather Q → Attention → A2A → LSE-reduce\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWith --dcp-replicate-q-proj:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    Hidden → [Replicated Q-proj on all ranks] → Attention → A2A → LSE-reduce\n             ↑ Skip AllGather, but compute Q-proj redundantly\"\u003e\u003cpre class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e    Hidden → [Replicated Q-proj on all ranks] → Attention → A2A → LSE-reduce\n             ↑ Skip AllGather, but compute Q-proj redundantly\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eImplementation phase:\u003c/strong\u003e This would be Phase 2 (after \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e--dcp-comm-backend\u003c/code\u003e in Phase 1 / PR \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3908719149\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34024\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34024/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34024\"\u003e#34024\u003c/a\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI've also updated \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3932952443\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34444\"\u003e#34444\u003c/a\u003e to focus purely on the \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e-tpa\u003c/code\u003e parameter design (see comment there). Let me know if this breakdown works!\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"1da0c20bc17cc196feade53acdc05659614d8f6bd4a305e2c1d93d4ba1feca80","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnFPZUUgAqjM4OTM2MDQxNDA="},{"node":{"__typename":"ClosedEvent","__isTimelineEvent":"ClosedEvent","databaseId":23263709623,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T15:02:00Z","actor":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTQxODY=","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8854186?s=64\u0026u=ea09464ea9d1523f09aa799c293fb42455410c54\u0026v=4","login":"LucasWilkinson","profileResourcePath":"/LucasWilkinson","__typename":"User","name":"Lucas Wilkinson"},"stateReason":"COMPLETED","duplicateOf":null,"closingProjectItemStatus":null,"closer":{"__typename":"PullRequest","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34883","number":34883,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","login":"vllm-project","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw"}},"__isNode":"PullRequest","id":"PR_kwDOI7xefs7Ezw_r"},"id":"CE_lADOI7xefs7o9BRhzwAAAAVqoAm3","intent":null,"__isNode":"ClosedEvent"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnLlevkABqzIzMjYzNzA5NjIz"},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":4294156432,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"sungsooha","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ0MDU="},"id":"I_kwDOI7xefs7o9BRh","number":34018,"locked":false,"databaseId":3908310113},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"huanpengchu","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42692242?v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/huanpengchu","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNjkyMjQy","name":"chuhp"},"id":"IC_kwDOI7xefs7_86CQ","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issuecomment-4294156432","createdAt":"2026-04-22T06:48:17Z","authorAssociation":"NONE","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2026-04-22T06:49:45Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"editor":{"__typename":"User","url":"https://github.com/huanpengchu","login":"huanpengchu","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNjkyMjQy"},"id":"UCE_lALOI7xefs7_86CQzrGnCeg"},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Hi, I'm from the Zhipu Infra team. Earlier this year, we implemented a Context Parallelism (CP) solution based on the Prefill/Decode, along with several optimizations.                                                                                                                                                                        \n                  \n                  \n  1. Communication-Computation Overlap — Effectively hide communication latency by overlapping it with computation.                                                                      \n  2. LSE Correction + All-to-All Fusion in Decode — Leverage symmetric memory to fuse LSE correction with All-to-All communication during the decode phase.                                                                                                                                                   \n  3. Cross-GPU KV Cache Storage (Interleaved Layout) — Support distributing KV cache across multiple GPUs in an interleaved layout for both prefill and decode phases, applicable to MLA and DSA scenarios.                                                                                                                                                              \n  4. Support batch_size \u003e 1 while using  CP in Prefill. The overall solution is also compatible with speculative decoding, PD , and radix cache.                                                                                                                                                  \n  5. Support different attention backend (flashinfer,flashmla,flashattention and so on).\n  6. Due to GPU memory constraints during the prefill phase, a portion of the weights is asynchronously loaded via H2D transfer or gathered via all-gather to obtain the full weights.\n                                                                                                                                                                                         \n                                                                                                                                                                                         \n  If the community has related requirements or use cases, I'd be happy to help with adaptation and integration.  ","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eHi, I'm from the Zhipu Infra team. Earlier this year, we implemented a Context Parallelism (CP) solution based on the Prefill/Decode, along with several optimizations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCommunication-Computation Overlap — Effectively hide communication latency by overlapping it with computation.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLSE Correction + All-to-All Fusion in Decode — Leverage symmetric memory to fuse LSE correction with All-to-All communication during the decode phase.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCross-GPU KV Cache Storage (Interleaved Layout) — Support distributing KV cache across multiple GPUs in an interleaved layout for both prefill and decode phases, applicable to MLA and DSA scenarios.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport batch_size \u0026gt; 1 while using  CP in Prefill. The overall solution is also compatible with speculative decoding, PD , and radix cache.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport different attention backend (flashinfer,flashmla,flashattention and so on).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDue to GPU memory constraints during the prefill phase, a portion of the weights is asynchronously loaded via H2D transfer or gathered via all-gather to obtain the full weights.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf the community has related requirements or use cases, I'd be happy to help with adaptation and integration.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"2f030ea7ffee53898e4af4ec624ecd459c9063968a4e507ea60a749451b8d586","isHidden":false,"viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","name":"vllm","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","id":"O_kgDOCCo5pw","login":"vllm-project","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"vllm-project/vllm","databaseId":599547518},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":2,"nodes":[{"__typename":"User","__isActor":"User","login":"YouNeedCryDear","name":"Arthur Cheng","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7149956?s=64\u0026u=3c4e1e289e6c799ad75c7a1497bda527ac30902a\u0026v=4","__isNode":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDk5NTY="},{"__typename":"User","__isActor":"User","login":"KevinZeng08","name":"Kevinzz","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76487593?s=64\u0026u=9f5f89078f821082c89f91a7cd058f72f484348a\u0026v=4","__isNode":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDg3NTkz"}]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABnbPyV2gAqjQyOTQxNTY0MzI="}]},"backTimelineItems":{"pageInfo":{"hasPreviousPage":true,"startCursor":null},"totalCount":12,"edges":[]}}},"safeViewer":null}},"timestamp":1789357531}]},"title":"Issue","appPayload":{"initial_view_content":{"can_edit_view":true},"current_user":null,"current_user_settings":{"preferred_emoji_skin_tone":null,"copilot_show_functionality":false,"use_single_key_shortcut":false},"paste_url_link_as_plain_text":false,"base_avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com","help_url":"https://docs.github.com","sso_organizations":null,"current_sso_orgs_match_dismissed_cookie":null,"multi_tenant":false,"tracing":false,"tracing_flamegraph":false,"catalog_service":"github/issues","scoped_repository":{"id":"R_kgDOI7xefg","owner":"vllm-project","name":"vllm","is_archived":false,"has_projects_enabled":true},"saved_views":null,"best_match_sort_enabled":false,"sidebar_expanded":true,"issue_search_type":"ISSUE_HYBRID","transactionalMessageBanner":null,"copilotSurveyBanner":null,"enabled_features":{"use_pull_request_subscriptions_enabled":false,"pull_request_single_subscription":true,"disable_issues_react_ssr":false,"copilot_natural_language_github_search":false,"private_avatars":false,"reserved_domain":true,"notifyd_issue_watch_activity_notify":false,"notifyd_enable_issue_thread_subscriptions":false,"timeline_best_effort_count_optimization":false,"copilot_auto_assign_metadata":false,"copilot_workspace_cross_repo_selection":false,"copilot_agent_mode":false,"issues_react_force_turbo_nav":false,"issues_react_client_side_caching":false,"copilot_swe_agent":false,"react_version_mismatch_detection":false,"issues_react_graceful_not_found_handling":false,"issue_create_relationships":false,"issues_relates_to_issues_search":false,"milestone_closed_issues_prioritization":true,"tasklist_block":false,"issues_create_semantic_similarity_analytics":false,"semantic_similarity_duplicate_issue_detection":true,"issue_cca_visualization":false,"scribe_artifacts_api":false,"issues_relates_to_relationship":true,"issues_relates_to_semantic_suggestions":false,"issue_pinned_views":true,"issue_pinned_views_team_vs_personal":false,"repo_issues_board_view":false}}}</script>
  <div data-target="react-app.reactRoot"><link rel="preload" as="image" href="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634405?u=5885b3c604d462fa7772c21d9c6f8d531ade9fdb&amp;v=4&amp;size=48"/><!--$--><!--$--><div class="IssueShowPage-module__issueDetailContainer__DbXfA"><div class="primary-viewer IssueDetail-module__IssueDetailContainer__JnqVq" data-testid="issue-viewer-container"><!--$--><div class="IssueViewer-module__issueViewerContainer__Hualk IssueViewer-module__mainContainer__lmFuF"><!--$--><div class="ArtifactsPanelLayout-module__Layout__Un04j" data-artifacts-panel-open="false" data-testid="issue-artifacts-panel-layout"><div style="--spacing:var(--spacing-none)" class="prc-PageLayout-PageLayoutRoot--KH-d" data-component="SplitPageLayout" data-has-sidebar="true"><div class="prc-PageLayout-SidebarWrapper-kLG4B ArtifactsPanelLayout-module__SidePanel__lCPFB ArtifactsPanelLayout-module__HiddenSidePanel__Dt0MK" style="--spacing-column:var(--spacing-none)" data-is-hidden="false" data-position="end" data-sticky="true"><div class="prc-PageLayout-VerticalDivider-9QRmK prc-PageLayout-SidebarVerticalDivider-0Rl0V" data-component="PageLayout.VerticalDivider" data-variant="none" data-position="end" style="--spacing:var(--spacing-none)"></div><div class="prc-PageLayout-Sidebar-iciWg" data-component="SplitPageLayout.Sidebar" style="--spacing:var(--spacing-none);--pane-min-width:450px;--pane-max-width:768px;--pane-width-custom:544px;--pane-width-size:var(--pane-width-custom);--pane-width:544px"><div class="height-full"></div></div></div><div class="prc-PageLayout-PageLayoutWrapper-2BhU2" data-width="full"><div class="prc-PageLayout-PageLayoutContent-BneH9"><div data-component="SplitPageLayout.Content" class="prc-PageLayout-ContentWrapper-gR9eG ArtifactsPanelLayout-module__Content__aDOuB" data-is-hidden="false"><div class="prc-PageLayout-Content-xWL-A" data-width="full" style="--spacing:var(--spacing-none)"><div class="ArtifactsPanelLayout-module__IssueContent__z8sBO"><div clas