;s profile"><img data-component="Avatar" class="prc-Avatar-Avatar-0xaUi" alt="@sungsooha" width="24" height="24" style="--avatarSize-regular:24px" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634405?u=5885b3c604d462fa7772c21d9c6f8d531ade9fdb&amp;v=4&amp;size=48" data-testid="github-avatar"/></a></div><div class="ActivityHeader-module__narrowViewportWrapper__n_VAC IssueBodyHeader-module__narrowViewportWrapper__iLs_y"><div class="IssueBodyHeader-module__titleSection__dX9cz"><a class="IssueBodyHeaderAuthor-module__authorLoginLink__aTls_ prc-Link-Link-9ZwDx" data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/sungsooha" data-testid="issue-body-header-author">sungsooha</a></div><div class="ActivityHeader-module__footer__HD8mP IssueBodyHeader-module__footerSection__Df7HB"><span>opened </span><a class="IssueBodyHeader-module__dateLink__kYTxQ prc-Link-Link-9ZwDx" data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34018#issue-3908310113" data-testid="issue-body-header-link"><relative-time class="IssueBodyHeader-module__RelativeTime__xv0lw" data-component="RelativeTime">on Feb 6, 2026</relative-time></a></div></div><div class="ActivityHeader-module__narrowViewportWrapper__n_VAC IssueBodyHeader-module__actionsWrapper__D4Syp"><div class="ActivityHeader-module__edits__pnYtu IssueBodyHeader-module__editsSection__nQnXE"></div><div class="IssueBodyHeader-module__badgesSection___PWtJ"><div class="IssueBodyHeader-module__badgeGroup__EPYnd"></div><div class="IssueBodyHeader-module__actionsSection__gnoaX"><button data-component="IconButton" type="button" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0" class="prc-Button-ButtonBase-9n-Xk prc-Button-IconButton-fyge7" data-loading="false" data-no-visuals="true" data-size="small" data-variant="invisible" aria-labelledby="_R_7tar97f9jl_" id="_R_dar97f9jl_"><svg data-component="Octicon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" class="octicon octicon-kebab-horizontal" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" display="inline-block" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:text-bottom"><path d="M8 9a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 0-3 1.5 1.5 0 0 0 0 3ZM1.5 9a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 0-3 1.5 1.5 0 0 0 0 3Zm13 0a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 0-3 1.5 1.5 0 0 0 0 3Z"></path></svg></button><span class="prc-TooltipV2-Tooltip-tLeuB" data-direction="s" data-component="Tooltip" aria-hidden="true" id="_R_7tar97f9jl_">Issue body actions</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class="IssueBodyViewer-module__IssueBody__xbjV0" id="issue-body-viewer" data-testid="issue-body-viewer"><div data-testid="markdown-body" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" class="markdown-body" data-turbolinks="false"><div class="markdown-body NewMarkdownViewer-module__safe-html-box__ZT1eD"><h3 dir="auto">Motivation.</h3>
<p dir="auto">This RFC proposes adding <strong>Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism</strong> to vLLM, based on <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07120" rel="nofollow">NVIDIA's Helix paper</a> (July 2025). Helix enables efficient long-context decoding by combining Context Parallelism (sequence sharding) with Tensor Parallelism (head sharding), eliminating KV cache duplication that occurs in traditional Tensor Parallelism when <code class="notranslate">TP &gt; num_kv_heads</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Paper results (NVIDIA):</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Up to <strong>1.5× decode latency reduction</strong> at fixed batch size</li>
<li>Up to <strong>32× more concurrent users</strong> at same latency target</li>
<li>Communication overhead <strong>O(B × H)</strong>, independent of sequence length</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Key benefits for vLLM:</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Eliminates KV cache replication</strong> when TPA &gt; num_kv_heads, improving memory efficiency</li>
<li><strong>Reduces memory pressure</strong> for long-context workloads (256K+ tokens)</li>
<li>Enables scaling MLA (DeepSeek) and GQA (Llama, Qwen) models more efficiently</li>
</ul>
<h2 dir="auto">Motivation</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">The Problem: KV Cache Duplication</h3>
<p dir="auto">Modern LLMs increasingly use <strong>MLA</strong> (Multi-head Latent Attention) or <strong>GQA</strong> (Grouped Query Attention) to reduce KV cache memory. However, these architectures have few KV heads:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Model</th>
<th>Attention</th>
<th>KV Heads</th>
<th>Problem with TP=8</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>DeepSeek-V2/R1</td>
<td>MLA</td>
<td>1 (effective)</td>
<td>8× KV duplication</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Llama-3 70B/405B</td>
<td>GQA</td>
<td>8</td>
<td>1× at TP=8, 4× at TP=32</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Qwen2.5</td>
<td>GQA</td>
<td>4-8</td>
<td>2-8× duplication</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto">When <code class="notranslate">TP &gt; num_kv_heads</code>, traditional TP must <strong>duplicate</strong> the KV cache across GPUs, wasting memory bandwidth during decode.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">vLLM's Current DCP and KV Cache Efficiency</h3>
<p dir="auto">vLLM's Decode Context Parallelism (DCP) helps by sharding KV cache along the sequence dimension. DCP works functionally with any TP/DCP combination, but there's a <strong>KV cache efficiency</strong> consideration:</p>
<p dir="auto">In standard DCP with TP=32, K=8, DCP=4:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Each DCP rank has TPA=8 Q heads but only HKVP=2 KV heads</li>
<li>AllGather Q brings all 32 Q heads to every rank</li>
<li>Each rank computes attention for all 32 Q heads against its 2 local KV heads</li>
<li>This effectively replicates each KV head 4× across TPA</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">This KV replication increases memory pressure for long-context workloads. The replication factor grows as TPA/K increases.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Proposed Change.</h3>
<h2 dir="auto">Proposed Solution: Helix (Context + Tensor) Parallelism</h2>
<p dir="auto">Helix decouples attention and FFN parallelism, allowing the same N GPUs to "twist" between two configurations each layer:</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="Attention Phase:  KVP × TPA  (KVP = sequence sharding, TPA = head sharding)
FFN Phase:        TPF × EP   (standard tensor/expert parallelism)"><pre class="notranslate"><code class="notranslate">Attention Phase:  KVP × TPA  (KVP = sequence sharding, TPA = head sharding)
FFN Phase:        TPF × EP   (standard tensor/expert parallelism)
</code></pre></div>
<h3 dir="auto">Key Difference from DCP</h3>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Aspect</th>
<th>Standard DCP</th>
<th>Helix</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Communication</td>
<td>AllGather Q + ReduceScatter</td>
<td><strong>All-to-All + LSE</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Q distribution</td>
<td>AllGather to all ranks</td>
<td>Distributed by TPA</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>KV efficiency</td>
<td>Replicates when TPA &gt; K</td>
<td><strong>No replication</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>GQA at TP=32, K=8</td>
<td>Works but 4× KV replication</td>
<td>✅ No replication (TPA=8, KVP=4)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<h3 dir="auto">Data Flow</h3>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="Input → QKV Proj → FlashAttn (local KV) → All-to-All → LSE Reduction → Output Proj → AllReduce
        (redundant)  + LSE                 (exchange)   (exact softmax)"><pre class="notranslate"><code class="notranslate">Input → QKV Proj → FlashAttn (local KV) → All-to-All → LSE Reduction → Output Proj → AllReduce
        (redundant)  + LSE                 (exchange)   (exact softmax)
</code></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">The All-to-All exchanges partial attention outputs with their log-sum-exp (LSE) values, enabling mathematically exact attention reconstruction across KVP ranks.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Feedback Period.</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>
<h3 dir="auto">CC List.</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Any Other Things.</h3>
<h2 dir="auto">Roadmap</h2>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Phase</th>
<th>Description</th>
<th>Dependencies</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>1. Core Helix (MLA)</strong></td>
<td>All-to-All + LSE reduction for MLA models</td>
<td>None</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>2. GQA Support</strong></td>
<td>Extend Helix to GQA models beyond KV head constraint</td>
<td>Phase 1</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>3. A2A Optimization</strong></td>
<td>Optimized All-to-All implementation</td>
<td>Phase 1</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto">Phase 1 is the prerequisite; Phases 2 and 3 can proceed in parallel.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Design Principles</h2>
<ol dir="auto">
<li><strong>Minimal new parameters</strong> - Single <code class="notranslate">helix_mode</code> flag; reuse existing <code class="notranslate">tensor_parallel_size</code> and <code class="notranslate">decode_context_parallel_size</code></li>
<li><strong>Reuse DCP infrastructure</strong> - KV interleaving, slot mapping, rank groups all compatible</li>
<li><strong>Feature parity</strong> - Support same models/backends as DCP</li>
</ol>
<h2 dir="auto">API Design</h2>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-python notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="from vllm import LLM

# Enable Helix for long-context MLA model
llm = LLM(
    model=&quot;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite&quot;,
    tensor_parallel_size=8,
    decode_context_parallel_size=4,  # KVP = 4
    helix_mode=True,                 # Enable Helix (All-to-All)
)

# For GQA model beyond KV head limit (Phase 2)
llm = LLM(
    model=&quot;meta-llama/Llama-3-70B&quot;,
    tensor_parallel_size=32,
    decode_context_parallel_size=4,  # Would not work with standard DCP
    helix_mode=True,                 # TPA=8, KVP=4
)"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-k">from</span> <span class="pl-s1">vllm</span> <span class="pl-k">import</span> <span class="pl-c1">LLM</span>

<span class="pl-c"># Enable Helix for long-context MLA model</span>
<span class="pl-s1">llm</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">LLM</span>(
    <span class="pl-s1">model</span><span class="pl-c1">=</span><span class="pl-s">"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite"</span>,
    <span class="pl-s1">tensor_parallel_size</span><span class="pl-c1">=</span><span class="pl-c1">8</span>,
    <span class="pl-s1">decode_context_parallel_size</span><span class="pl-c1">=</span><span class="pl-c1">4</span>,  <span class="pl-c"># KVP = 4</span>
    <span class="pl-s1">helix_mode</span><span class="pl-c1">=</span><span class="pl-c1">True</span>,                 <span class="pl-c"># Enable Helix (All-to-All)</span>
)

<span class="pl-c"># For GQA model beyond KV head limit (Phase 2)</span>
<span class="pl-s1">llm</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">LLM</span>(
    <span class="pl-s1">model</span><span class="pl-c1">=</span><span class="pl-s">"meta-llama/Llama-3-70B"</span>,
    <span class="pl-s1">tensor_parallel_size</span><span class="pl-c1">=</span><span class="pl-c1">32</span>,
    <span class="pl-s1">decode_context_parallel_size</span><span class="pl-c1">=</span><span class="pl-c1">4</span>,  <span class="pl-c"># Would not work with standard DCP</span>
    <span class="pl-s1">helix_mode</span><span class="pl-c1">=</span><span class="pl-c1">True</span>,                 <span class="pl-c"># TPA=8, KVP=4</span>
)</pre></div>
<h2 dir="auto">Alternatives Considered</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">1. Extend DCP to support TP &gt; num_kv_heads</h3>
<p dir="auto">Would require duplicating KV heads across ranks, defeating the purpose of context parallelism.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">2. Ring attention</h3>
<p dir="auto">Higher latency for decode phase due to sequential send/recv chain. All-to-All provides lower latency when all GPUs have direct connectivity (NVSwitch).</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Related Work</h2>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Helix Paper:</strong> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07120" rel="nofollow">arXiv:2507.07120</a> - Original Helix parallelism paper (NVIDIA, July 2025)</li>
<li><strong>vLLM DCP:</strong> Existing decode context parallelism in vLLM</li>
<li><strong>Related vLLM RFCs:</strong>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693/hovercard">#22693</a> - Context Parallelism &amp;&amp; Sequence Parallelism</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133/hovercard">#26133</a> - Context Parallelism with Fully Sharded KV Cache and Ring Attention</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Differentiation:</strong> While <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3312280381" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693/hovercard" href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/22693">#22693</a> and <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3478786804" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133/hovercard" href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/26133">#26133</a> use ring attention for context parallelism, Helix uses <strong>All-to-All</strong> communication which provides lower latency on NVSwitch-connected systems and removes the <code class="notranslate">TP ≤ num_kv_heads</code> constraint for GQA models.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Before submitting a new issue...</h3>
<ul class="contains-task-list">
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" id="" disabled="" class="task-list-item-checkbox" aria-label="Completed task" checked=""> Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the <a href="https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/" rel="nofollow">documentation page</a>, which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.</li>
